<br/>In answer to Barry:
<br/>
<br/>The answer is....
<br/>....from the mushroom royalty: LION''S MANE Hericium erinaceus or, depending on foklore - yamabushitake (= ‘mountain priest mushroom’), bearded tooth fungus, bearded hedgehog, or old man''s beard
<br/>
<br/>Sliced and quickly fried in a film of oil with salt and a touch of garlic and ta-ta! Your brain sparkles and become sharp not to mention other multiple benefits known and unknown yet to humans
<br/>The other ones are the chestnut mushrooms, delicious also, cooked the same and with a bit of lemon on top</td>', 'If I got the last place with these mushrooms with a grand pedigree it means that people might want to try some to reap their benefits

In answer to Barry:

